{%- comment -%}
  box-border-edges — the classes a border asks for: one `bt-/bb-/bl-/br-` per edge that draws, plus
  the role class colouring them. `box-border-style` is the value half and a caller needs both.

  An edge's WIDTH is a space tier, so `theme_variables` emits its class beside `pt-`/`mt-`/`gap-`
  and `value_by_bp` makes the edge responsive with no axis of its own. Colour and style stay shared
  across edges (`--border` / `--border-style`); across 1,002 bordered elements no source names two
  edges apart, so a per-edge colour would buy nothing.

  Emits NOTHING where no edge states a width — the edges ARE the border, so there is no mode beside
  them, and a caller gates its style half on this being blank.

  Inputs:
    top / right / bottom / left — a space tier id per edge, blank where that edge draws nothing
    role — border_role. A SLOT role emits `border-<role>`, which reads that slot's variable;
           'palette' / 'custom' / 'none' read `--border`, which the style half writes for the first
           two and leaves unset for the third; 'gradient' needs `border-gradient` because
           border-color cannot take one. Passing NO role is the opt-out for a caller painting the
           colour through a custom property of its own — it emits no colour class at all.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign edge_classes = blank -%}
{%- assign has_edge = false -%}
{%- if top != blank and top != 'none' -%}
  {%- assign edge_classes = edge_classes | push: 'bt-{{ top }}' -%}
  {%- assign has_edge = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if bottom != blank and bottom != 'none' -%}
  {%- assign edge_classes = edge_classes | push: 'bb-{{ bottom }}' -%}
  {%- assign has_edge = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if left != blank and left != 'none' -%}
  {%- assign edge_classes = edge_classes | push: 'bl-{{ left }}' -%}
  {%- assign has_edge = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if right != blank and right != 'none' -%}
  {%- assign edge_classes = edge_classes | push: 'br-{{ right }}' -%}
  {%- assign has_edge = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if has_edge -%}
  {%- if role == 'gradient' -%}
    {%- assign edge_classes = edge_classes | push: 'border-gradient' -%}
  {%- elsif role == 'none' or role == 'custom' or role == 'palette' -%}
    {%- comment -%}All three paint through `--border`, which `.border-default` reads as transparent when unset.{%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign edge_classes = edge_classes | push: 'border-default' -%}
  {%- elsif role != blank and role != 'none' and role != 'custom' and role != 'palette' -%}
    {%- assign edge_classes = edge_classes | push: 'border-{{ role }}' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {{- edge_classes | join: ' ' -}}
{%- endif -%}
